 "notes": "Libretto by Lorenzo Da Ponte (1787). Words follow the Schirmer vocal score's spelling and punctuation: \"ciglio\" with the print's accent the first time (bar 15), \"ciglio\" the second; \"di asciugar\" sung as di‿asciugar on one note (libretto \"d'asciugar\"); \"vogl'io\" on one syllable, except in bars 85-86 where the print splits it as \"vogl'\" and \"io\"; the repeats (\"andate, andate\", \"cercate\" four times, \"a vendicar io vado\" twice, \"nunzio vogl'io tornar\" and \"sì\") as printed. IPA, word meanings and translations were drafted for this app (S48) and the IPA was checked against Castel. Don Ottavio sings the two quatrains twice through. IPA follows sung Italian conventions: stressed syllable marked, elisions (two words on one note in the score) joined with ‿, open e/o as ɛ/ɔ; \"io\" on a single note is jo, \"io\" carrying several notes ˈi.o. Translation literal, for meaning.",
